{"id":"5e01a0ed-5d26-4c85-830a-5fb44c4c3ccb","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"5a9a78ff9d156efb","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/index.ts","baseline":{"blob":"907be0b8f8c5347569816c644f02eeb5b0a6a826","start":2467,"end":2625},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","implementations","=","import",".","meta",".","glob","<","CommandFactory",">","(","[","\"","./commands/*/*.ts","\"",",","\"","!./commands/*/command.ts","\"",",","\"","!./commands/**/*.test.*","\"","]",",","{","\"","import","\"",":","\"","create","\"","}",")"]},"context":{"before":"c36977c20bb47eb8","after":"8f915f09145d037f"}},"payload":{"text":"Each command's implementation (`commands/<name>/<name>.ts`), loaded the first time the command runs.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:11:04.957Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:11:04.957Z"}
{"id":"63e42a32-5d1c-407f-b3ae-2d2a9cddc82a","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"e702a2dca82f767f","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/index.ts","baseline":{"blob":"2431f5026b8db18d86b7316e1f6d06b106abfd6b","start":11793,"end":12574},"shape":{"type":"If","atoms":["if","(","runner",".","isRunning","(",")",")","{","if","(","code","===","0x","0D","||","code","===","0x","0A",")","{","fire","(","\"","\\","\\r\\n","r","\\","n","\"",")",";","runner",".","sendStdin","(","`","","${","stdinBuffer","}","\\","\\n","n","`",")",";","stdinBuffer","=","\"","","\"",";","}","else","if","(","code","===","0x","7F","||","code","===","0x","08",")","{","if","(","stdinBuffer","!==","\"","","\"",")","{","stdinBuffer","=","stdinBuffer",".","slice","(","0",",","-","1",")",";","fire","(","\"","\\","\\b \\b","b","\\","b","\"",")",";","}","}","else","if","(","code","===","0x","04",")","{","if","(","stdinBuffer","===","\"","","\"",")","{","runner",".","endStdin","(",")",";","}","else","{","runner",".","sendStdin","(","stdinBuffer",")",";","stdinBuffer","=","\"","","\"",";","}","}","else","if","(","code",">=","0x","20","||","code","===","0x","09",")","{","fire","(","character",")",";","stdinBuffer","+=","character",";","}","}"]},"context":{"before":"12ff2a83f892c7ac","after":"01d262f84e41bb4b"}},"payload":{"text":"(a non-node command is running: only Ctrl-C reaches it)","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:09:05.318Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:09:05.318Z"}
{"id":"725ae7c3-a3e8-4e8a-8a70-c95e07da2193","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"a4eb2d27eddc588a","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/index.ts","baseline":{"blob":"0cb053b51f22919e10bec4a8dbf047c30b5a75c7","start":38,"end":84},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","Hub","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/hub","\""]},"context":{"after":"1cf547f97e8d1cbe"}},"payload":{"text":"The workspace terminal — just-bash (a pure-TS bash interpreter) on the editor's own filesystem (fs.ts), with the\neditor's own commands beside its (catalog.ts: a folder each under commands/ — `node` runs a program in the debugger,\nthrough node-runner.ts). It IS the default terminal: the editor\nregisters this as the vendored backend's process factory (setTerminalProcessFactory, in workbench-entry), so\nevery terminal the workbench opens is this one — `> tsconfig.json` hits the read-only guard (permission denied)\nand files the shell creates show up in the explorer.\n\nSession model — and DON'T \"fix\" the probe below thinking it's a workaround for using just-bash wrong: it is\nstateless per `exec` BY DESIGN (each call is a one-shot, isolated run, so a `cd`/`export` doesn't stick; only the\nfilesystem, being external, persists). just-bash's OWN interactive shell\n(`just-bash-shell`) has the identical limitation — it calls `Bash.exec(line)` exactly like we do, and `cd`/\n`export` don't persist across its prompts either. There is no persistent-session API to use instead. So the\ninteractive session layer is ours to add: we hold cwd + env here and thread them through every `exec`. env\nround-trips via the result (`BashExecResult.env` — the only state just-bash returns); cwd is read back with a\n`$PWD` probe appended to each command — the same technique VS Code's own shell integration uses (emit `$PWD`\nafter each command), and semantically correct (it captures the top-level shell's final dir and respects\nsubshell isolation, which intercepting `cd` would not) — see session.ts. One line editor, one prompt, sync\ninput handling.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:11:10.004Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:11:10.004Z"}
{"id":"7b6beacf-ece3-42c2-84de-b1f89e163d57","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"9b01e10980809607","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/index.ts","baseline":{"blob":"c1ea2839af0597b7fb2ad8c02e1818f5ac5dcc7b","start":5055,"end":5109},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","state",":","SessionState","=","{","\"","cwd","\"",":","cwd0",",","\"","env","\"",":","{","}","}"]},"context":{"before":"6953134d9001a499","after":"6467bcdf6b7fcebd"}},"payload":{"text":"The session: cwd + env, carried from command to command (session.ts).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:10:24.434Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:10:24.434Z"}
{"id":"7de15dd2-4cf0-4baf-ba33-f61c5f477eed","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"98b62ba659024a0f","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/index.ts","baseline":{"blob":"a90069cfff7b247adac81b112bd5e72eeb25dfd0","start":2956,"end":3041},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["let","completions",":","string","[]","=","[","...","BUILTINS",",","...","COMMANDS",".","map","(","(","command",")","=>","command",".","name",")","]"]},"context":{"before":"8f915f09145d037f","after":"57ce6c6f888fc8f5"}},"payload":{"text":"What Tab offers in command position: the shell's builtins, just-bash's commands (as this build has them — no\n`tar` in a browser), and ours. Known once just-bash has loaded (with the first command, or warmed at start).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:10:49.832Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:10:49.832Z"}
{"id":"838b54b3-fb4a-4f9c-baa1-2ceb315b24c7","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"05fb130f038e1980","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/index.ts","baseline":{"blob":"634c5e00826f14219015cb6738e40dc4248e854f","start":3758,"end":3775},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","TAIL","=","8000"]},"context":{"before":"adaa2ef5e0d7ffce","after":"a52afd7978ea1260"}},"payload":{"text":"How much of a terminal's output is kept, its latest: what an agent reads of it (debug-mcp's `terminal`).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:10:39.628Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:10:39.628Z"}
{"id":"8d757197-6dd7-4f38-a381-b5b723b56e79","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"02320028df95c1a1#17","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/index.ts","baseline":{"blob":"8c213f212415d9ecc58d2e45801166be50ee0f87","start":20493,"end":20499},"shape":{"type":"Keyword","atoms":["return"]},"context":{"before":"1a899df1918846ee","after":"9b39e75172362b67"}},"payload":{"text":"The terminal closing stops what it's running — a dev server, a script — rather than leaving it running unseen.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:07.795Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:07.795Z"}
{"id":"8eaef068-7fa1-467b-a500-a136e92fbf6f","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"3e7b78b23f5a6c44","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/index.ts","baseline":{"blob":"79e10c55ece70594ae37e846ff99591f17058562","start":8445,"end":8461},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["let","fresh","=","true"]},"context":{"before":"e6fd7bbcf950545d","after":"6b1c2f1ed01187ab"}},"payload":{"text":"Whether what's been written for this line ends a line: a statement's output after another's goes on a new one.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:09:42.614Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:09:42.614Z"}
{"id":"9636f221-55c2-4a24-8f2a-20738ec967c7","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"a52afd7978ea1260","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/index.ts","baseline":{"blob":"979f4eb78efce477391b89e6772352adb2acd603","start":3890,"end":3998},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","tails","=","new","Map","<","number",",","{","\"","terminal","\"",":","number",";","\"","command","\"","?",":","string",";","\"","open","\"",":","boolean",";","\"","text","\"",":","string","}",">","(",")"]},"context":{"before":"05fb130f038e1980","after":"4145ce6da620b6b0"}},"payload":{"text":"Each terminal's latest output (ANSI escapes stripped), by its number — and whether it's still open, and the one\ncommand it runs (a task's). VS Code's extension API can't read a terminal's buffer, but every byte it shows goes\nthrough here.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:10:29.594Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:10:29.594Z"}
{"id":"a455f72a-0d64-46ae-b657-936bb68d8a37","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"fd9fa232c39a6d25","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/index.ts","baseline":{"blob":"b9bfd0d1b6959c45692670f2f577efd74436883e","start":9318,"end":9411},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","statements","=","statementsOf","(","input",",","STREAMING",")","??","[","{","\"","text","\"",":","input",",","\"","then","\"",":","\"","","\"","as","const","}","]"]},"context":{"before":"6b1c2f1ed01187ab","after":"9a90aaa0293d5037"}},"payload":{"text":"A line with a streaming command (`node`) runs a statement at a time (session.ts statementsOf): just-bash\nhands back a line's output only when the whole line's done, so what came before the command would otherwise\nshow after it. `;`, `&&` and `||` keep their meaning: a statement after `&&` runs if the last one ran succeeded,\nafter `||` if it failed. Any other line runs whole.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:09:31.927Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:09:31.927Z"}
